comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T12:45:42.822Z",codex-sol,"Reproduced the issue ESM script verbatim in a new empty npm project with pm-context@2026.10.10 and @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.11 (Node v24.19.0). All four kinds retain their raw relationship but produce a.dependsOn=[b], b.dependedBy=[a]. related and implements falsely imply scheduling; blocks reverses execution order; blocked_by passes as the positive control. Agent output literally reports a: depends_on [b]. Imported only issue 136 atomically after duplicate searches and two dry runs selecting exactly one issue using --since 2026-10-11T10:07:00Z. UX gaps: github import offers no issue-number or limit selector; bare pm install pm-github fails and requires npm:pm-github. No extension installation state will be committed."
  "2026-10-12T12:45:44.690Z",codex-sol,"Plan: resolve registered relationship definitions and use the SDK ordering orientation primitive for derived dependency summaries. Keep association, implementation, unknown kinds, raw edges and neighborhood context unchanged. Add public builder and installed CLI JSON/Markdown/agent regressions using real scratch trackers, including extension-defined semantics and byte-preservation checks. Prove failure by reverting only the projection and rebuilding before running the new tests."
  "2026-10-12T12:49:23.452Z",codex-sol,"Implementation uses the public registry ordering flag and precedence contract, whose omitted precedence defaults to source_before_target. The SDK orientation helper exists internally but is not exported through the public package entry points, so no internal SDK imports were introduced. Pure builder callers may supply relationshipRegistry; both commands resolve the active workspace registry. Regression fixtures install copied dist and manifest files into real scratch trackers; discovery ignores symlink-only extension roots."
  "2026-10-12T12:53:28.882Z",codex-sol,"Additional SDK/CLI gaps encountered while building extension-kind regressions: the host create --dep argument validator rejects registered custom relationship kinds as outside its built-in enum, and ItemMetadata dependency kinds are typed as the built-in union. The regression therefore imports extension-owned metadata with the real public commitImportedItem writer and tests active custom semantics through actual installed CLI commands. Scratch item IDs use the tracker prefix returned by the SDK. These host gaps are outside issue 136 and will be reported without filing changes elsewhere."
  "2026-10-12T12:56:25.507Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only the dependency-projection loop in buildContextPack with its origin/main implementation; retained new tests, registry option and command wiring. Ran npm run build, then node --test test/dependency-projection.test.ts: 15 tests, 3 pass, 12 fail, zero skipped/cancelled/todo, exit 1. Failures include association-only, implementation-only, inverse blocks, mixed edges, and active custom semantics through installed CLI output. The blocked_by and depends_on controls pass. Restored the fixed projection and rebuilt dist. Earlier fixed focused run passed all 15 tests; final linked and release gates follow."
  "2026-10-12T12:58:23.419Z",codex-sol,"Fixed linked regression verification passed: pm test pm-context-github-356cb2a080ed-136 --run --progress executed npm run build && node --test test/dependency-projection.test.ts successfully. All 15 regression tests pass, zero fail/skipped/cancelled/todo, including the registered temporal non-ordering recurs_from control. Item documents and history streams remain byte-identical through installed CLI serving. npm run build:test and npm run docstring also pass. Release checks will use a clean HOME with global/system Git config disabled."
  "2026-10-12T13:02:24.870Z",codex-sol,"Release gates passed at unchanged thresholds: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and the same environment with bun run release:check each pass 316/316 tests, zero fail/skipped/cancelled/todo. Each reports 100.00% lines, branches and functions over the configured six-source scope; typecheck, release workflow, docstrings, audit (zero vulnerabilities), package dry-run and attestation/date checks pass. The Bun command runs the repository-defined gate chain, whose test suite uses Node. No coverage thresholds, dependencies or extension installation state changed. Claim will be released with the item left in_progress for orchestrator verification; changelog regeneration/check and PR follow."
  "2026-10-12T13:03:17.776Z",codex-sol,"npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check both pass after the recorded gates and claim release. CHANGELOG.md remains byte-identical because the imported issue stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. Only this issue item/history pair, the projection implementation, regression tests, public documentation and rebuilt dist files are included. No other issues were imported and no package installation state is tracked. Preparing the PR with Fixes #136 and the canonical pm item link."
  "2026-10-13T12:31:32.584Z",codex-agent,"Review fix round: verify registered ordering behavior, add real-tracker regression coverage and behavioral revert proof, merge the current base, rebuild committed dist, and run npm and Bun release gates. Review threads and bots will not be contacted."
  "2026-10-13T12:39:22.587Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the outside-diff finding: handoff blockers rejected incoming source-before-target edges before interpreting registered precedence. Handoff builder and renderer now accept the registry, command paths supply active definitions, and raw kinds are retained independently of includeDeps. Added real temporary-tracker regressions for blocks, custom ordering/default precedence/aliases, contextual kinds, focus exclusion, next actions, agent output and durable-byte preservation. Current base is already incorporated."
  "2026-10-13T12:49:57.962Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: kept tests and command registry wiring unchanged, restored only buildAgentHandoff from the PR head, and rebuilt dist. The focused command node --test --test-name-pattern=handoff.blockers test/dependency-projection.test.ts failed 2/2: both includeDeps modes omitted the incoming blocks prerequisite. The expanded fixed baseline passed 2/2 with built-in and custom raw-kind assertions. Restored the fixed function and rebuilt. Linked test timeout was raised to 2400 seconds for shared-host execution without changing any quality threshold."
  "2026-10-13T13:36:58.993Z",codex-agent,"Final clean-identity gates passed at unchanged thresholds. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 318 tests, 318 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, 0 skipped and 0 todo. Coverage is 100% lines, branches and functions across the six configured sources: index.ts, context-receipts.ts, context-usage.ts, and the coverage, docstring and publish-attestation scripts. Production audit found 0 vulnerabilities. Typecheck, release workflow, docstrings, pack dry-run, publish attestation and changelog-date checks passed. The Bun command runs the repository gate chain; the test suite executes under Node. The focused handoff regression passed 2/2 after the fix was restored. Reverting only buildAgentHandoff and rebuilding dist failed both includeDeps modes because the incoming blocks prerequisite was omitted. Item remains in_progress."
  "2026-10-13T15:54:36.214Z",pi-agent,"History restoration round: CI health on the earlier review-fix push failed both Node matrix jobs because this item's history chain and item hash did not verify under the then-pinned 2026.10.10 host (history_drift; upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1458) - a newer host had written the 12:41 tests_update entry with a context the older pinned host rejects. The earlier response was to re-anchor the stream: history records 21-26 were REPLACED with versions recomputed by the pinned 2026.10.10 host plus a history_repair marker, and the item document lost its per-test updated_by/updated_at fields. That violates the append-only contract, so this change restores the original records 21-26 and the matching item document byte-exactly from the last pre-re-anchor commit (SHA-256 identical on both files), drops the recomputed replacements and the repair marker entirely, and bumps the @unbrained/pm-cli devDependency pin to 2026.10.13 so CI's pinned host verifies the newer-host tests_update entry instead of history being rewritten. The only genuinely new content added by the re-anchor commit was its CI-failure note, whose substance is preserved in this comment. Verified under the bumped pinned host: history --verify ok (26 entries, item hash matches the last restored record) and health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exits 0 with history_drift ok."
  "2026-10-13T16:05:47.273Z",pi-agent,"Gates after the restoration and pin bump, at unchanged thresholds and clean CI identity: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass with 318 tests, 318 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, 0 skipped, 0 todo. Coverage 100.00 percent lines, branches and functions across the six configured sources. Production audit found 0 vulnerabilities. Typecheck, release workflow verification, docstring gate, committed-dist freshness, package dry-run, publish attestation and changelog-date checks all pass; changelog:full leaves CHANGELOG.md byte-identical and changelog:check passes. Linked evidence rerun under the bumped pinned host: the dependency-projection regression suite passed 17/17, and the linked history-verify command passed (26 restored entries plus the appended restoration records, item hash matching the chain head)."
  "2026-10-13T16:06:44.414Z",pi-agent,Delivered as a single commit on the PR branch restoring the original item/history pair and bumping the @unbrained/pm-cli devDependency pin to 2026.10.13 (package.json and package-lock.json; no other dependency or threshold changed). The history stream now contains the 26 restored original records plus only appended restoration records; the diff against the restored commit has zero deletions. PR body updated with the restoration round and the item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification; claim released.
